.TH GIT-AUTOSYNC 1 "2026-09-01" "git-autosync 2.15" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-autosync \- Git automatic synchronization toolkit (auto-sync local folders with Gitee/GitHub)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-autosync
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGUMENT\fR]
.br
.B git-autosync
.RI ( without arguments, opens the interactive main menu )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-autosync
automatically syncs local folders to Gitee / GitHub, or periodically pulls
remote repositories to local directories.
.PP
This is a Linux port of the Windows v2.15 version (PowerShell + NSSM). It uses
.B systemd
instead of NSSM services, and
.B inotifywait
instead of FileSystemWatcher for real-time file watching, with feature parity
with the original version.
.PP
Run without any arguments to enter the interactive main menu, which exposes all
functionality. The menu defaults to English; a Chinese mode is available via the
.I Language
option.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B env
Environment check: git, inotify-tools, SSH private key, systemd, python3.
.TP
.B ssh-key
Generate an SSH key (ed25519) and print the public key to add to Gitee / GitHub.
.TP
.B new
Create a new auto-push repository (local \(-> remote). Interactively asks for the
SSH private key, commit identity, local path, excluded directories, platform and
remote address; then creates and enables the systemd service
.BR git-autosync@<name>.service .
.TP
.B remove
Remove a push directory: untrack the specified subdirectory and add it to
.gitignore, keeping local files.
.TP
.B mirror
Create a new cloud mirror pull (remote \(-> local): register the remote address
and local directory; may clone once immediately.
.TP
.B fetch-timer
Periodic pull service management: enable/disable, set interval (minutes), run once.
.TP
.B list
List all registered repositories and their service status.
.TP
.B status
Show detailed status of each repository service.
.TP
.BR start " | " stop " | " restart " | " enable " | " disable " <name>"
Start / stop / restart / enable at boot / disable the sync service of the named repository.
.TP
.B uninstall \fR<name>
Uninstall the sync service of the named repository; repository files are kept by default (optional full removal).
.TP
.B fix
Fix all sync services: clean stale index.lock files and restart.
.TP
.B rebuild
Fully rebuild all services (stop \(-> reinstall units \(-> re-enable).
.TP
.B mail
Email notification wizard: bind SMTP, toggle notifications, send test mail, manage recipients, set notification interval.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/git-autosync/
Program files (bin, lib, systemd, docs).
.TP
.I /etc/git-autosync/repos/<name>.conf
Per-repository sync configuration. Fields:
repo_path, branch, remote, ssh_key, debounce, retry, retry_wait, mail_notify, log_file, exclude.
.TP
.I /etc/git-autosync/mirror_config.txt
Mirror pull registry, one line per entry:
.BR "target_dir|remote_url|branch|ssh_key_path" .
.TP
.I /etc/git-autosync/mirror_settings.txt
Pull settings:
.BR interval=60 ", " default_ssh_key= .
.TP
.I /etc/git-autosync/mail_config.txt
SMTP mail configuration (mode 0600): enabled, smtp_server, smtp_port, use_ssl, from, password, to, notify_interval.
.TP
.I /var/log/git-autosync/
Pull log mirror_fetcher.log, mail log git_mail_notify.log.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/git-autosync@.service
Push service template (one instance per repository).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GIT_MIRROR_CLEAN=0
Do not clean untracked files when pulling.
.TP
.BR GIT_AUTOSYNC_PREFIX ", " GIT_AUTOSYNC_CONF ", " GIT_AUTOSYNC_LOG
Override the default install, config and log directories (for debugging).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
First-time setup in three steps:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo git-autosync env       # 1. Environment check
sudo git-autosync ssh-key   # 2. Generate SSH key
sudo git-autosync new       # 3. Create an auto-push repository
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspect service status and logs:
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemctl status git-autosync@myrepo.service
journalctl -u git-autosync@myrepo.service -f
tail -f /path/to/repo/git_sync.log
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR inotifywait (1),
.BR git (1)
.PP
